# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 1 of the Tutorial

[B11's Example 5.7]

e,1,0,36
r1,1,2,1'k
r2,2,3,3'k
r3,3,0,2'k

analysis: dc
note: The first simulation in the tutorial: a series circuit, described and solved step by step in Lesson 1. Find the resistance seen by the source, the source current, the voltage drop across each resistor, the power delivered by the source and the power consumed by each resistor. The Evaluate line checks the power balance: the resistors consume exactly what the source delivers, so the four powers come to zero.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/circuit/b11e0507.jpg
rounding: 3
si: yes
units: yes
evaluate: pr1 + pr2 + pr3 + pe


[HK5's Figure 1-26]

e1,1,0,120
r1,1,2,30
e2,2,3,30
r2,3,0,15

analysis: dc
note: Find the current, voltage drop and power consumed in each resistor, and the power delivered by each voltage source; then check that all the powers add up to zero. The 30 V source consumes 60 W rather than delivering it, which is why -pe2 comes out negative.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/hk5s-figure-1-26-1.jpg
rounding: 3
si: yes
units: yes
evaluate: pr1 + pr2 + pe1 + pe2


