[RM3's Example 7-5 (Hidden source)]

e1,1,0,12.
r1,1,b,10
r2,b,a,10
r3,a,2,50
r4,b,2,30
e2,2,0,-6

analysis: dc
note: In this problem, we meet a 'hidden source' for the first time: the schematic shows no source symbol, only labelled supply voltages, so the description introduces one source for 12 V and one for -6 V. Find the indicated currents and the voltage Vab.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/rm3s-example-7-5-hidden-source-17.jpg
rounding: 3
si: yes
units: yes
evaluate: va-vb


[RM3's Figure 7-16 (Hidden source)]

r1,1,b,4'k
r2,1,a,3'k
r3,b,a,2'k
r4,b,a,3'k
r5,1,b,1'k
rt,a,2,6'k
e1,1,0,-2
e2,2,0,-10

analysis: dc
note: Another hidden-source circuit, with supplies of -2 V and -10 V. Find the total circuit resistance, and the indicated currents and voltages. Also evaluate va-vb, which is -0.8 V.
